# Git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default. The container
# entrypoint is copied straight into a Linux image, where CRLF makes it
# unrunnable (`/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`) and kills the API container on
# startup. Pin the working tree to LF on every platform so a clone behaves the
# same wherever `docker compose up` is run.
* text=auto eol=lf
